WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.270
A theatre.

2
00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.840
The front row has twenty seats.

3
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.790
Every row behind has two more
seats than the row in front.

4
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.890
Twenty, twenty-two,
twenty-four, and on it goes.

5
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.920
There are thirty rows in all.

6
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.760
So how many seats are there altogether?

7
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.290
Do you count every row, one by one?

8
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.960
Or is there a shortcut?

9
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:24.300
In this mission, you'll
spot an arithmetic sequence:

10
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.400
the same amount added each time,
called the common difference.

11
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:34.340
You'll find any term with u n equals
u one plus n minus one, times d.

12
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:39.650
Then you'll add a whole series fast, by
pairing the first term with the last.

13
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: work out how many
seats there are in thirty rows.
